# Infrastructure agent project

Dome dependency, templates, and skill: {{.Version}}. Start with the `dome` skill
in `.agents/skills/dome/SKILL.md`. This project defines topology in Go and loads
values through typed YAML; do not introduce a runtime infrastructure DSL.

Optionally use the generated `.devcontainer/` through Dev Container CLI or VS
Code, running at `/workspace` with container Go. Local Go is also supported;
keep subsequent agent runs in the same environment and project path.

Build/test and inspect `./agent plan --json` before applying. Apply host changes
when requested by the user. Preserve existing configuration and ownership. Keep
secrets out of identifiers, logs, errors, snapshots, and execution metadata.

When delivering this agent to a customer, include corresponding source,
dependency versions, build instructions, and configuration. Establish customer
control of repositories and deployment keys without publishing secrets. The
customer must be able to modify/rebuild independently or use another provider.
